"""upgrade-walk: the whole ecosystem on the vault upgrade, walked end to end on a running devnet.

docs/plans/yellowback-upgrade-plan.md §4 (the bridge), §5 (YED on the primitive), §15.8 (the
set_* / vault_* RPCs) and §15.10 (U-21..U-24), exercised on the one-laptop devnet with every
client the devnet runs: chain-viz, lightwalletd (the fork, --yellowback) and yolo beside pool 4.
Every step prints the calls it makes and the evidence (txids, RPC outputs) into a transcript
(--transcript, default <dir>/upgrade-walk-transcript.txt) and ends PASS or stops at the first
FAIL. The checklist this script follows is scenarios/upgrade-walk.md.

The devnet it expects (deterministic: nothing mines but this script):

    yellowback-devnet up --role attestor --no-heartbeat --no-walk --no-sim --seed 480

Eleven nodes: 0 the minter, 1 stock (no attestor set: the YED module is inert there, the
primitive is not), 2-4 pools (real quote agents), 5-7 attestors, 8 the empty attestor seat this
walk fills (join, mature, agent, heartbeat), 9 a holder, 10 the claimant.

Steps (each can be skipped with --skip NAME[,NAME]):
  clients    lightwalletd (fork, --yellowback) on --lwd-port, yolo beside pool 4, chain-viz probe
  members    attestor set membership: node 8 joins, matures, heartbeats; node 6 goes dormant (S15)
             with its agent stopped and revives with a SET_HEARTBEAT when it comes back
  mint       arming (ARMED, seated), mints -> the V template (tag YED, the attestor set, CLAIM_DELAY)
  transfer   yed_send to the holder and the claimant
  redeem     the owner redeems at lockHeight (selector 2; in term it is open too, quoted with the
             early-redeem fee, IT-9); renew = redeem + mint the same debt
  claim      $5 crash: an underwater claim -> claimant intent (CLAIMING); a reorg across it; release
             after CLAIM_DELAY (CLAIMED)
  cancel     a wrong-price claim cancelled by one attestor: burn lost, the vault ACTIVE again
  interm     an in-term claim (in-term claims plan IT-1/IT-2/IT-7): the price falls until a class-A
             vault crosses theta in term; a claim above theta is refused everywhere, the claim at
             theta accepted, released after the delay, the residual to the owner, one state hash;
             owner redeems in term (D-IT-15) paying the early-redeem fee (IT-9: 5 % of the collateral
             for class A), above theta (G) and under it, pre-empting a claim (H). SKIPs unless
             yed_getinfo.params.inTermClaims is true
  invalid    an invalid mint refused by every Yellowback mempool, the block carrying it rejected by
             every Yellowback node
  bridge     the WYEC bridge persona (bridge-sim) in both shapes: lock -> mock burn -> intent ->
             release; a rogue intent cancelled; owner recovery when the guardians fall silent
  final      one state hash on every node (YED and vault), chain-viz and lightwalletd agree

    ../.venv/bin/python contrib/yellowback/devnet/upgrade-walk [--dir DIR] [--transcript PATH] [--skip ...] [--summary PATH]
"""
